    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Clarke Auctioneers Ltd are delighted to present \"Cosy Cottage\", this charming two-bedroom semi-detached cottage, occupying a substantial site in the heart of the picturesque village of Glenealy, Co. Wicklow. Full of character and warmth, this delightful home offers the perfect blend of traditional cottage charm and village convenience, complemented by an extensive rear garden with exceptional potential for extension, landscaping or further enhancement (subject to the necessary planning permission).\n\nBeautifully maintained by its current owners, the property provides bright, well-proportioned accommodation and represents an outstanding opportunity for first-time buyers, those looking to downsize, or anyone seeking a peaceful village lifestyle within easy reach of Wicklow Town, Ashford and the M11 motorway.\nOn arrival, the property immediately impresses with its attractive traditional façade, framed by low stone boundary walls and a traditional cottage front garden. A graveled driveway provides convenient off-street parking to the rear of the property.\n\nInternally, the accommodation is both welcoming and full of character. The entrance hallway leads to a comfortable sitting room overlooking the front and side gardens. This bright and inviting living space is centered around a charming wood-burning stove, creating a warm and cosy atmosphere throughout the year.\n\nThe property comprises two bedrooms, positioned to the front and rear respectively, both offering comfortable and well-proportioned accommodation. To the rear of the home, the kitchen/dining room overlooks the private rear garden and is fitted with an excellent range of floor and eye-level kitchen units, tiled flooring and ample space for everyday dining. A practical utility room provides additional storage and laundry facilities.\n\nThe family bathroom is neatly presented and fully functional, while also offering purchasers the opportunity to modernise and personalise to their own taste.\n\nOne of the property`s most appealing features is the extensive rear garden. Enjoying an excellent level of privacy, this generous outdoor space offers enormous scope to create a superb family garden, outdoor entertaining area or substantial extension to the existing dwelling, subject to the appropriate planning permissions. Whether your vision is a landscaped garden, home office, workshop or additional living accommodation, the possibilities are extensive.\n\nProperties combining such character, generous site size and a prime village-centre location rarely come to the market. Early viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate everything this charming home has to offer."
      },
